---
/**
 * ============================================================================
 * src/pages/gated/[...slug].astro — Paywalled post body ("gated" route)
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * WHAT THIS IS
 *   A statically-generated Astro page that emits the FULL rendered body of
 *   every paywalled ("gateable") blog post at build time, one HTML file per
 *   post under the /gated/<slug> URL space (e.g. /gated/my-paid-essay/).
 *
 * SINGLE RESPONSIBILITY
 *   Render the complete post content — nothing else. It carries no paywall
 *   logic, no auth checks, no UI chrome (no header/footer/layout). It is a
 *   bare content fragment whose ONLY job is to exist as a build artifact that
 *   the edge middleware can serve to entitled readers.
 *
 * HOW IT FITS THE ARCHITECTURE (why a separate route exists at all)
 *   The public post page (src/pages/blog/[...slug] or similar) ships only a
 *   teaser/preview plus the <PaywallGate> component. The paid body is NOT in
 *   that HTML — otherwise anyone could "View Source" and read it for free.
 *   Instead the paid body lives here, under /gated/*, and access is enforced
 *   at the EDGE by functions/gated/_middleware.js (a Cloudflare Pages
 *   Function). The request flow:
 *
 *     reader → GET /gated/<slug>
 *            → functions/gated/_middleware.js intercepts FIRST
 *                • validates the reader's access token (signature + expiry)
 *                • checks the Supabase entitlement (did they pay for THIS post?)
 *                • honors admin bypass (is_admin()) for the owner's own preview
 *            → only on success does it let Cloudflare Pages return the static
 *              HTML that THIS file generated.
 *
 *   So the security boundary is the middleware, not this page. This page is
 *   "dumb" on purpose: keeping gate logic out of the static asset means the
 *   asset is safe to cache and impossible to partially leak.
 *
 * SECURITY ASSUMPTIONS / GOTCHAS (read before touching anything)
 *   1. THE MIDDLEWARE IS THE ONLY GUARD. If functions/gated/_middleware.js is
 *      removed, renamed, or its matcher stops covering /gated/*, these fully
 *      rendered paid bodies become world-readable static files. Do not move
 *      this route out from under the middleware's path.
 *   2. NO SECRETS IN CONTENT. Because the output is a plain static file behind
 *      an edge check (not per-user rendered), never assume anything here is
 *      private beyond the token/entitlement gate. It's the whole post, served
 *      as-is to anyone the middleware admits.
 *   3. SEARCH / SITEMAP LEAK VECTORS. Paid bodies must never surface in the
 *      public search index or sitemap, or the text would leak via those
 *      indexes even though the page itself is gated. This is defended in two
 *      places: `data-pagefind-ignore` below (Pagefind skips the node), and
 *      the sitemap/RSS config excludes the /gated/* path. Both must stay true.
 *   4. NO DRAFTS, GATEABLE ONLY. getStaticPaths filters to gateable && !draft
 *      so we don't accidentally build a /gated page for a post that isn't
 *      meant to be sold, and don't publish unfinished drafts to the edge.
 *
 * DEPENDS ON
 *   - astro:content — getCollection('blog') + render() (Astro content layer).
 *   - The 'blog' content collection schema, which must define the booleans
 *     `gateable` and `draft` used in the filter below.
 *
 * DEPENDED ON BY
 *   - functions/gated/_middleware.js — gates access to these built files.
 *   - The public post page's <PaywallGate>, which points entitled readers at
 *     the corresponding /gated/<slug> URL to fetch/reveal the paid body.
 * ============================================================================
 */
import { getCollection, render } from 'astro:content';

// Full body of gateable posts. Served ONLY through functions/gated/_middleware.js,
// which verifies the reader's token + entitlement. data-pagefind-ignore keeps this
// content out of the public search index; it's also excluded from the sitemap.
//
// getStaticPaths runs at BUILD time and enumerates which /gated/<slug> pages to
// generate. The predicate is a security-relevant allow-list:
//   • data.gateable  — only posts explicitly flagged as sellable get a gated body.
//   • !data.draft    — never emit a gated body for an unfinished/unpublished draft.
// `post.id` (the collection entry id, i.e. the slug) becomes the [...slug] param,
// and the full entry is forwarded via `props` so we don't re-fetch it below.
export async function getStaticPaths() {
  const posts = await getCollection('blog', ({ data }) => data.gateable && !data.draft);
  return posts.map((post) => ({ params: { slug: post.id }, props: { post } }));
}

// `post` arrives from getStaticPaths props (no runtime query needed). render()
// compiles the post's Markdown/MDX into an Astro <Content /> component using the
// full pipeline (Shiki syntax highlighting, KaTeX math, build-time D2 diagrams,
// etc.) — the exact same body a paying reader is entitled to see. NOTE: any
// interactive cells the body contains (client-side Pyodide/Plotly "python"
// plots, notebook-style stdout) ship as inert markup + hydration scripts here
// and only come alive in the reader's browser AFTER the middleware serves this
// fragment; nothing in this pipeline runs per-user at request time.
const { post } = Astro.props;
const { Content } = await render(post);
---

{/*
  The ONLY output of this page: the fully-rendered paid body, nothing else.
  - id="gated-body" is the stable hook the client-side PaywallGate looks for when
    it swaps the teaser for the real content after the middleware serves this file.
  - data-pagefind-ignore tells the Pagefind indexer to skip this subtree so the
    paid text never enters the public search index (leak vector #3 above).
  No layout/header/footer here on purpose — this is a content fragment, and the
  edge middleware is what decides whether the fragment is ever delivered.
*/}
<div id="gated-body" data-pagefind-ignore><Content /></div>
